# Build context is the repository root. Everything here is either unusable in
# the image, or actively harmful to ship into one.
#
# The .venv exclusion is the one that matters most: it is a full local
# virtualenv built for this host, hundreds of megabytes, and it would be sent
# to the daemon on every build only to be overwritten by the one uv builds.

# --- virtualenvs and caches ---
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- version control and editors ---
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- secrets: the image takes its configuration from the environment ---
# .env.example is kept: it is documentation, not configuration.
.env
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# --- runtime state, regenerated in the container ---
logs/
**/logs/
src/assets/
**/qdrant_db/

# --- not part of the application ---
test/
Docker/
skills/
README.md
LICENSE
pytest.ini
*.md
